phase#aResultOverTheBoundIsCutAndNamed| ITEM: #688 fix-issue-688-loop-spend · the state records phase A · base 3dc0ddfafc43
phase#aResultOverTheBoundIsCutAndNamed| CHECKLIST: /home/tim/projects/NaviVeylin/.pi/worktrees/loop/tools/loop/prompts/worker.md
phase#aResultOverTheBoundIsCutAndNamed| ## Phase A — root cause and the red test
phase#aResultOverTheBoundIsCutAndNamed| 
phase#aResultOverTheBoundIsCutAndNamed| 1. Verify the entry against the tree. Confirm the condition still holds, with a `file:line`, and that it
phase#aResultOverTheBoundIsCutAndNamed|    is not already fixed. If it no longer holds, stop: verdict `skipped`, sub-verdict `stale`, with the
phase#aResultOverTheBoundIsCutAndNamed|    `file:line` that shows the claim is gone. A stale claim carries no measurement and no review, so the run
phase#aResultOverTheBoundIsCutAndNamed|    does not retire the item on it: it escalates it, and your `LOOP-DECISION` is the question a person answers —
phase#aResultOverTheBoundIsCutAndNamed|    retire it as stale, or re-diagnose it. When the `ITEM_CHANGE` block names a change, this step verifies
phase#aResultOverTheBoundIsCutAndNamed|    *that* change's claims first: a cited `file:line` that moved, or a red case that is green on the base, is
phase#aResultOverTheBoundIsCutAndNamed|    `needs-diagnosis` naming the path, not an invitation to plan again.
phase#aResultOverTheBoundIsCutAndNamed| 2. Name the root cause in one sentence: the single mechanism that explains the symptom. Two mechanisms
phase#aResultOverTheBoundIsCutAndNamed|    means the item is not eligible — verdict `skipped`, sub-verdict `needs-diagnosis`. For `{{PROPOSE_CLASS}}`
phase#aResultOverTheBoundIsCutAndNamed|    there is no root cause to name: name the one missing capability and the `file:line` (or the named run)
phase#aResultOverTheBoundIsCutAndNamed|    that shows it is absent, and treat two independent missing capabilities as `needs-diagnosis`.
phase#aResultOverTheBoundIsCutAndNamed| 3. Produce the **red test**: the smallest case that exercises the defect and fails on HEAD. Record the
phase#aResultOverTheBoundIsCutAndNamed|    JUnit XML `tests=`/`failures=`, the case name and the timestamp. For a non-defect, the red case
phase#aResultOverTheBoundIsCutAndNamed|    asserts the number, count or absence the delta requires — never "better". For `{{PROPOSE_CLASS}}`, the
phase#aResultOverTheBoundIsCutAndNamed|    red case is the acceptance scenario the new requirement states: it fails on HEAD because the capability is
phase#aResultOverTheBoundIsCutAndNamed|    absent, and it passes only once the capability exists.
phase#aResultOverTheBoundIsCutAndNamed| 4. Name the owning capability and the owning guideline section. Route with `AGENTS.md`'s Documentation
phase#aResultOverTheBoundIsCutAndNamed|    Map; never read a guideline in full.
phase#aResultOverTheBoundIsCutAndNamed| 5. Count the surface before the plan is fixed. The rule you are about to change has more than one place that
phase#aResultOverTheBoundIsCutAndNamed|    asserts it, and the plan is only real once you know how many: `tools/look.sh '<the rule>'` names the files that
phase#aResultOverTheBoundIsCutAndNamed|    hold the rule's text and its symbol — over the cases (`tools/*-cases.sh`), the engine, the prompts and the
phase#aResultOverTheBoundIsCutAndNamed|    fixtures — and lists the cases and fixtures that assert the behaviour being changed. The proposal carries the count with the command that produced it
phase#aResultOverTheBoundIsCutAndNamed|    (`surface: 2 cases added, 2 rewritten, 4 fixtures realigned — <command>`), because the count, not the first
phase#aResultOverTheBoundIsCutAndNamed|    file the plan names, is what the estimate is set against. An estimate made before this pass is the defect
phase#aResultOverTheBoundIsCutAndNamed|    this step exists for: the #232 change was planned as two functions and landed as 292 insertions over six
phase#aResultOverTheBoundIsCutAndNamed|    files (issue #238).
